# Force LF everywhere. This is not style - it is correctness.
#
# docs/world_model_architecture.md defines
#   data_hash = sha256(canon(sim) + canon(data) + arm_blocks.xml)
# so the scene XML's raw bytes enter the provenance hash. A CRLF/LF split would
# make one scene produce two different data_hash values and silently fork E-4's
# provenance chain. Everything runs natively on Windows now - WSL2 cannot render
# here and is out - but the rule stays: git's autocrlf, an editor, or a future
# checkout on another OS can each reintroduce the split on their own.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact inputs to hashes and comparisons.
*.xml  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Generated blobs. Gitignored, but declare intent in case one is ever forced in.
*.pixels binary
*.meta   binary
